{"type":"cards","design":"S66_CARDS_PHOTO_STRIP","title":"SQL Server licensing optimization in DR","items":[{"title":"BYOL license mobility","text":"License transfer: existing Microsoft SQL Server Enterprise licenses with active Software Assurance migrate directly to Google Cloud Compute Engine VMs without re-purchasing core entitlements.","icon":"shield-dollar"},{"title":"Passive replica rights","text":"Zero-cost DR cores: Software Assurance permits one passive failover replica in the secondary DR region with zero additional SQL Server core licenses while it runs no read workloads.","icon":"cloud-database"},{"title":"Custom machine shapes","text":"Core ratio tuning: Compute Engine custom machine types decouple vCPU count from memory capacity, matching high buffer-pool RAM demands while minimizing licensed SQL Server cores.","icon":"gear-dollar"},{"title":"Sole-tenant node options","text":"Physical core binding: dedicated sole-tenant nodes support physical core licensing and host-level isolation when Contoso Health compliance policies or legacy agreements require dedicated hardware.","icon":"hex-lock"}],"notes":"We optimize Contoso Health's Microsoft licensing footprint by combining Bring Your Own License mobility under Software Assurance with passive disaster recovery replica rights. Because the secondary DR replica remains passive during normal operations, it incurs compute and storage charges only, while custom machine types keep active vCPU counts aligned with actual query CPU demand.

