{"type":"process","design":"S66_BANNER_NUMBERED_ROWS","title":"Post-outage failback and resynchronization","items":[{"title":"Rebuild failed primary region infrastructure","text":"Provision replacement Compute Engine instances or repair existing nodes in the original primary region. Validate Persistent Disk integrity, Active Directory connectivity, and WSFC node health before rejoining the cluster."},{"title":"Re-establish async replication to original primary","text":"Resume data movement from the active DR primary back to the restored primary region nodes in asynchronous commit mode. Monitor transaction log send and redo queues until synchronization lag reaches zero."},{"title":"Switch to synchronous mode during maintenance","text":"Coordinate a scheduled maintenance window with Contoso Health clinical operations. Transition the replication mode between the active DR node and the restored primary node from asynchronous to synchronous commit."},{"title":"Execute planned manual failover to primary","text":"Verify both regions report a synchronized state with zero data loss exposure. Issue a planned manual failover command, update Cloud DNS back to the primary internal load balancer, and revert DR to asynchronous mode."}],"notes":"Returning operations to the primary Google Cloud region after a disaster requires re-establishing replication in reverse before cutting traffic back. Switching temporarily to synchronous commit mode during a planned maintenance window ensures zero data loss when executing the final manual failover back to the primary region.

